  "priorRegistries": [],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "name": "RevC1Counters",
      "agent": "reviewer",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nAttack the C1 counters: run `bash <lane>/corpus/instruments/r40-closure.sh --export-ref <Y> --work $S/w --lane /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin` (Y = the lane tip) and record the full output and exit; it must print `closed=10/10 exit=0`. Then `--selftest --export-ref <Y>` must print `selftest cases=10 failures=0` with 10 graded case lines. Then the two negative controls: `--export-ref a7af2ce63bce153757d39bf66b366a96caf30c13` and `--export-ref 8371e7ac9f32cae5ed72f8c28205634603f836fa` must print closed<10/10 exit=1, and a plain run must exit 2. Also verify the suite file's sha256 equals the SKILL.md Gates & probes registry row. Attack: try to make a check pass while its defect is present by supplying a modified export (e.g., patch the exported SOURCES/records) in scratch — if any check stays green under a defeater, that is a defect. Deliver the transcripts + verdict.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability, coverage\nMilestone: round-40 falsify wave 2: attack C1 suite/counters, C2 decisions/rows/entries, sources re-open, junk controls\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-40/wave2/RevC1Counters.md"
    },
    {
      "name": "RevC1Sandbox",
      "agent": "reviewer",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nAttack the r40 suite's sandbox: (1) export with a symlink inside the tree pointing outside it; (2) export with a path traversal candidate (a file named `../evil` or a declared block path containing `..`); (3) reuse a `--work` dir that already contains a previous export (stale-state trick); (4) run with `--scratch-root` pointing at a dir containing unrelated kasegi-r4* stray dirs (must red) and with an empty scratch root (must green). Record each run's output. Any check reading the live lane instead of the export, or passing with stale/unrelated state, is a defect. Deliver transcripts + verdict.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability, coverage\nMilestone: round-40 falsify wave 2: attack C1 suite/counters, C2 decisions/rows/entries, sources re-open, junk controls\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-40/wave2/RevC1Sandbox.md"
    },
    {
      "name": "RevH2Corrections",
      "agent": "reviewer",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nAttack the H2 target: verify at Y that `grep -c '^Correction (round 40)'` is >=1 in each of SCORECARD.md, LOG.md, SHONEN.md and corpus/lessons/round-39.md, and that each such line names the final r39 receipt values (`closed=7/8 exit=1` and `selftest failures=1`) and the G2/G6 non-independence reason. Also verify the corrections are pure appends (previous claimed untouched). Any record still claiming r39 C1 8/8 at Y without the correction is a defect. Deliver counts + verdict.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability, coverage\nMilestone: round-40 falsify wave 2: attack C1 suite/counters, C2 decisions/rows/entries, sources re-open, junk controls\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-40/wave2/RevH2Corrections.md"
    },
    {
      "name": "RevH3Criterion",
      "agent": "reviewer",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nAttack the H3 target: verify `grep -cE 'M39-2' corpus/QUALITY.md` >=1 at Y and that the criterion row is grounded (cites the lesson row and states the receipt-transcript rule). Flag a criterion that names the class without citing M39-2 (R36). Deliver output + verdict.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability, coverage\nMilestone: round-40 falsify wave 2: attack C1 suite/counters, C2 decisions/rows/entries, sources re-open, junk controls\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-40/wave2/RevH3Criterion.md"
    },
    {
      "name": "RevH4GateRows",
      "agent": "reviewer",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nAttack the H4 target: read corpus/lessons/round-39.md's Gate section at Y and verify the S056/S058/S059 rejected-row blocks each carry a URL, an access date, and a <=25-word located quote. Re-locate each quote in the live source by fetching the URL (record status/bytes/sha256) and confirming the quote text occurs. Any block lacking any of the three, or a quote not matching the live source, is a defect. Deliver rows + verdict.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability, coverage\nMilestone: round-40 falsify wave 2: attack C1 suite/counters, C2 decisions/rows/entries, sources re-open, junk controls\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-40/wave2/RevH4GateRows.md"
    },
    {
      "name": "RevC2Decisions",
      "agent": "reviewer",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nAttack the C2 decision set at Y: verify each of the nine rows S016/S017/S019/S020/S021/S022/S023/S024/S025 has status `mined` or `rejected` (queued count must be 0); verify the lesson's old→new change-log line exists for each; verify S022's flip names S030 and S024's flip names S029; verify mined rows each have exactly one knowledge entry citing them and rejected rows each carry reason+flip in the row (`teaches` cell). Count mined among the nine (must be >=4). Any queued row, missing log, or evidence-free decision is a defect. Deliver the per-row table + verdict.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability, coverage\nMilestone: round-40 falsify wave 2: attack C1 suite/counters, C2 decisions/rows/entries, sources re-open, junk controls\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-40/wave2/RevC2Decisions.md"
    },
    {
      "name": "RevC2Entries",
      "agent": "reviewer",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nAttack the C2 knowledge entries: for each mined entry among the nine decided rows (and any S060+ mined entry), run `python3 <lane>/corpus/instruments/source-recheck.py --manifest <lane>/corpus/source-snapshots/round-40/manifest.json --source S###` and record exits; verify each entry passes QUALITY Q1-Q6 (provenance trio; tier A/B support; <=25-word located quotes; attribution; a falsifiable rule + a rejected over-generalization; documentation-only, no credentials). Re-open one quote per entry in the capture. Any entry failing Q1-Q6 or a recheck non-zero is a defect. Deliver per-entry verdicts.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability, coverage\nMilestone: round-40 falsify wave 2: attack C1 suite/counters, C2 decisions/rows/entries, sources re-open, junk controls\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-40/wave2/RevC2Entries.md"
    },
